        "date": "2026-11-21T12:33:26Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): guided sheet job - stock, Z zero, allowance, XY zero, clamp clearance\n\nOne undoable SetSheetJob runs the existing SetStock and SetWcsOrigin\nand writes a new SetupDef::sheet_job record; one undo restores all\nthree. The post gate refuses by name a move below the sheet bottom\nless the stated through-cut allowance, a rapid across below the sheet\ntop plus the clamp clearance, and a stock or Z zero edited after the\nchecklist. The record saves additively; the loader refuses a value the\ncommand would refuse. MCP set_sheet_job (allowance and z_zero required,\nget_job shows the job) and a \"Sheet job\" group on a milling setup's\nSettings page drive the same command.\n\nFixes #3070\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
